ESP32-S3: come out of reset with CPENABLE=0xff, like the silicon.

This is the esp32s3 half of the fix qemu-espressif.nix already applies to
`hw/xtensa/esp32.c` by substituteInPlace (see espressif/qemu#154 and the
unmerged PR #155, whose note in that file says it "only fixes esp32s3" --
upstream, not in this release tarball, so the S3 machine still has it).

Espressif parts come out of reset with all coprocessors enabled, but the
generic xtensa `cpu_reset()` only sets CPENABLE under CONFIG_USER_ONLY.  In
system mode the guest's first FP instruction therefore traps Cp0Disabled,
and xtensa-lx-rt's `save_context` re-faults while spilling f0..f15 -- a
silent double exception.  On the S3 that showed up as an endless boot loop:
the app printed esp-rtos' "Main task created" and then reset with
`rst:0xc (RTC_SW_CPU_RST)`, over and over, with `_DoubleExceptionVector`
the last thing executed before the reset vector.

Applied after esp32s3-appcpu-stall.patch, which touches the same reset
block.

--- a/hw/xtensa/esp32s3.c
+++ b/hw/xtensa/esp32s3.c
@@ -216,11 +216,13 @@
         xtensa_select_static_vectors(&s->cpu[0].env, s->rtc_cntl.stat_vector_sel[0]);
         remove_cpu_watchpoints(&s->cpu[0]);
         cpu_reset(CPU(&s->cpu[0]));
+        s->cpu[0].env.sregs[CPENABLE] = 0xff;
     }
     if (s->requested_reset & ESP32S3_SOC_RESET_APPCPU && (ESP32S3_CPU_COUNT > 1)) {
         xtensa_select_static_vectors(&s->cpu[1].env, s->rtc_cntl.stat_vector_sel[1]);
         remove_cpu_watchpoints(&s->cpu[1]);
         cpu_reset(CPU(&s->cpu[1]));
+        s->cpu[1].env.sregs[CPENABLE] = 0xff;
